A functional interface is introduced in java8;

It can only have a single abstract method.

But it allows any number of static and default methods. 

A functional interface can be annotated with: 
@FunctionalInterface on top of Interface declaration

Lambda expression:
------------------
A lambda expression is a short way to write an implementation for 
functional interface.

It is introduced in Java 8.


It helps to reduce the boiler plate code.

Boiler plate code: 
-----------------
It is a code which is repetitive.


Lambda expressions can be used with functional interface, which 
contains only one abstract method.

Lambda expressions are commonly used with Collections, Streams 
and functional interfaces.

Syntax:
-------

(arguments)-> expression

The -> symbol is known lambda operator. 


